#F f1f2_WindtWithCompton.dat
#UT Elastic Photon-Atom Scattering, anomalous scattering factors, f2 corrected for Compton (incoherent) scattering.
#C  This file has been created using f1f2_Windt.pro
#D  Tue Sep 18 17:24:07 2001
#C  This file belongs to the DABAX library. More information on
#C  DABAX can be found at:
#C  http://www.esrf.fr/computing/scientific/dabax/
#UIDL xf1f2
#UD Elastic Photon-Atom Scattering, anomalous scattering factors.
#UD
#UD The scattering values in this file have been obtained from
#UD the IMD code from David Windt (windt@astro.columbia.edu):
#UD http://cletus.phys.columbia.edu/~windt/idl/
#UD
#UD The data are generated by concatenation of of data from
#UD CXRO (http://www-cxro.lbl.gov) and LLNL
#UD (http://www-phys.llnl.gov/V_Div/scattering/asf.html)
#UD
#UD Derived from f1f2_Windt.dat on 2026-09-25 by add_compton_all.py.
#UD For every element (H to U), f2 has been multiplied, energy
#UD point by energy point, by the correction factor
#UD     (mu_photo + mu_compt) / mu_photo
#UD where mu_photo and mu_compt are the photoelectric and Compton
#UD (incoherent) scattering cross sections for that element,
#UD computed with xraylib (CS_Photo, CS_Compt respectively). f2
#UD in this file therefore represents photoelectric + Compton
#UD absorption, instead of photoelectric absorption alone as in
#UD f1f2_Windt.dat. f1 is unchanged.
#UD At energies outside the range covered by xraylib's cross
#UD section tables (mostly at the low-energy end, below each
#UD element's tabulated range), the nearest valid correction
#UD factor is reused.
#UD
#UD Column description: 1:PhotonEnergy[eV]  2:f1  3:f2 (includes Compton correction)
#UD
#S  1  H
#UB -.999900
#UF1ADD 0.0
#N 3
#L PhotonEnergy[eV]  f1  f2
#UO ;  Atomic scattering factors for H.
#UO ;   
#UO ;  Concatenation of data from CXRO <http://www-cxro.lbl.gov>
#UO ;  and LLNL <http://www-phys.llnl.gov/V_Div/scattering/asf.html>
#UO ;  
#UO ;  E (eV) f1 f2
#UO ;  
#UO ;  f2 corrected for Compton (incoherent) scattering:
#UO ;  f2_new = f2 * (CS_Photo+CS_Compt)/CS_Photo  [xraylib]
#UO ;  see add_compton_all.py
#UO ;---------------
